WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.210
INFERIVA for development finance institutions: an overview.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.421
Development finance institutions invest directly, back sponsors,

00:00:09.421 --> 00:00:13.576
and lend through partner banks. Transactions are few and large.

00:00:13.576 --> 00:00:18.390
The risk is in who owns the counterparty, who stands behind the borrower,

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.622
and what the partner bank's files actually prove.

00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:26.120
Monitoring built for transaction speed misses that risk.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.109
What matters is due diligence that is evidenced,

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:33.779
screening that reaches owners and sponsors, and a record of every decision.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:39.642
Each partner bank has a file: its documents, each marked verified or pending,

00:00:39.642 --> 00:00:42.935
and its beneficial owners, with their shareholdings.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:48.233
Owners and sponsors are screened against sanctions and debarment lists,

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:51.293
with the list and the reason for each match recorded.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.063
A match escalates the counterparty to enhanced due diligence,

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:57.874
with the reason in plain words.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:03.002
The case records what has been asked for and what is still missing,

00:01:03.002 --> 00:01:06.585
so a credit decision rests on evidence, not on a declaration.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.778
Every decision is on record, with who made it and when, for your board,

00:01:11.778 --> 00:01:13.627
your funders and your regulators.

00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:18.800
Partner banks, owners, sponsors and due diligence, all on record.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.134
So when your board or your funders ask how you know, you can show them.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:27.004
To see it for your institution, talk to INFERIVA.
